  "issue": {
    "body": "From [https://www.starlette.io/templates/](https://www.starlette.io/templates/):\r\n```python\r\ntemplates = Jinja2Templates(directory='templates')\r\n```\r\nThis folder is relative to the working directory.  This could perhaps be more clearly stated in the documentation.  (This caught us off guard when it wasn't working in a dockerized environment)\r\n\r\nWe fixed it by doing:\r\n```python\r\ntemplates = Jinja2Templates(directory=__file__[:__file__.rindex('/') + 1] + 'templates')\r\n```\r\nThe relative to working directory is unexpected.  Perhaps something like what I have should also be provided in the documentation.",
    "closed_at": "2019-08-16T09:31:36Z",
    "created_at": "2019-08-08T23:11:53Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/595",
    "number": 595,
    "state": "closed",
    "title": "Jinja2Templates directory parameter is relative to working directory",
